10:  rat:{label:'Rat · hepatocyte',kind:'cell',species:'Rat (Rattus norvegicus)',cellType:'Hepatocyte · representative somatic cell',description:'A rat hepatocyte is a nucleated, metabolically active liver cell. This preset uses a synthetic genome and proxy measurements; it is not a rat genome or a predictive liver-cell model.',sources:[['Rat hepatocyte biology · NCBI Bookshelf','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK541055/'],['Mammalian red-cell enucleation review · PubMed','https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34378417/']],contrast:'Mature mammalian red blood cells, unlike this hepatocyte, normally lose their nucleus during development.'},
