13:  influenza:{label:'Influenza A · virion',kind:'virus',species:'Influenza A virus (IAV)',unit:'Virion',shape:'Enveloped, roughly spherical or pleomorphic particle with surface glycoprotein spikes.',genome:'Eight separate segments of negative-sense single-stranded RNA; the segments encode viral products and are packaged in the virion.',description:'Influenza A is an enveloped virus, not a cell. It has no nucleus, mitochondria, or independent cellular metabolism, and it does not divide. New virions are assembled in infected host cells.',sources:[['Influenza A virus entry, replication, assembly and movement · Frontiers','https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4483285/'],['Influenza virus genome organization · NCBI Bookshelf','https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK2263/']],host:'Infection and replication require susceptible host cells; the plate depicts extracellular virions only.'},
